## STEP 5 -- the same three operations on an UNRELATED subsystem: a layer-3 interface address

Subsystem A is a forwarding filter. If dynamic configuration were a property of the ACL engine
alone the requirement would not be met, so the same triple is now run on `interface vlan48`,
with `vlan10` as an untouched control.

### 5a -- CHANGE, in place, on a live interface

```
awplus(config)#interface vlan48
awplus(config-if)#ip address 10.38.22.70/27
awplus(config-if)#end                                 [box 14:18:17 NZDT]
```
Accepted with **no `% ` line** -- the address was **replaced in place**, not rejected as a
duplicate and not silently added as a secondary:
```
awplus#show ip interface brief                        [box 14:18:25, 8 s later]
vlan10                10.38.22.34/27     admin up        running    
vlan48                10.38.22.70/27     admin up        running    
```
and the DUT logged it itself:
```
2026 Oct 21 01:18:03 user.notice awplus NSM[913]: vlan48 installed address 10.38.22.70/27
```
(DUT UTC 01:18:03, which with the measured ~13 h 10 s offset is box ~14:18:13 -- i.e. **at the
moment the command was entered**, not at some later convergence.)

```
sudo arpleg.py --tag svi-change ... --iface eth4 --arp 10.38.22.66,10.38.22.70 \
     --icmp 10.38.22.66,10.38.22.70 ... --count 4
  cap svi-change-eth4.pcap: 33 frame(s)
    x4     ARP-REQ  who-has 10.38.22.66     tell 10.38.22.65
    x4     ARP-REQ  who-has 10.38.22.70     tell 10.38.22.65
    x4     ARP-REPLY 10.38.22.70     is-at e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43
    x4     ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.65     -> 10.38.22.66     [ours]
    x4     ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.65     -> 10.38.22.70     [ours]
    x4     ICMP t0/c0 10.38.22.70     -> 10.38.22.65     [ours]
    x4     ICMP t3/c1 10.38.22.70     -> 10.38.22.65     [ours]
    x3     ARP-REQ  who-has 10.38.22.66     tell 10.38.22.70
    x1     ARP-REQ  who-has 10.38.22.65     tell 10.38.22.70
    x1     ARP-REPLY 10.38.22.65     is-at 00:0d:b9:55:77:0f
```
**This is the exact mirror image of the STEP 1 baseline**, every flow inverted:

| probe | baseline (.66 configured) | after the change (.70 configured) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ARP who-has `.66` | **4 replies** | **0 replies** |
| ARP who-has `.70` | 0 replies | **4 replies**, from the same MAC |
| ICMP echo to `.66` | **4 echo replies** | 4 **host unreachable**, sourced from `.70` |
| ICMP echo to `.70` | 4 host unreachable, sourced from `.66` | **4 echo replies** |

Note the detail that makes this airtight: **the source address of the ICMP unreachable follows
the change too** (`.66` in the baseline, `.70` afterwards). The whole layer-3 identity of the
interface moved, in the dataplane, with no restart.

### 5b -- DELETION, with the control on the other interface

```
awplus(config)#interface vlan48
awplus(config-if)#no ip address 10.38.22.70/27
awplus(config-if)#end                                 [box 14:19:10 NZDT]
awplus#show ip interface brief                        [box 14:19:17]
vlan10                10.38.22.34/27     admin up        running    
vlan48                unassigned         admin up        running          <- gone
```
```
sudo arpleg.py --tag svi-del ... --iface eth4 --arp 10.38.22.66,10.38.22.70 \
     --icmp 10.38.22.66,10.38.22.70 ... --count 4
  cap svi-del-eth4.pcap: 16 frame(s)
    x4     ARP-REQ  who-has 10.38.22.66     tell 10.38.22.65
    x4     ARP-REQ  who-has 10.38.22.70     tell 10.38.22.65
    x4     ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.65     -> 10.38.22.66     [ours]
    x4     ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.65     -> 10.38.22.70     [ours]
```
**16 frames captured, 16 frames sent: NOTHING came back.** No ARP reply for either address and
-- the telling part -- **not even an ICMP unreachable**, because with no address on that subnet
the DUT has nothing to source one from. That is a qualitatively different silence from the
baseline's and from STEP 2's, and it is the correct one for "the address was deleted".

The control, in the same minute, on the interface this step did not touch:
```
sudo arpleg.py --tag svi-del-ctrl ... --iface eth3 --arp 10.38.22.34 --icmp 10.38.22.34 ... --count 4
  cap svi-del-ctrl-eth3.pcap: 16 frame(s)
    x4     ARP-REQ  who-has 10.38.22.34     tell 10.38.22.33
    x4     ARP-REPLY 10.38.22.34     is-at e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43
    x4     ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.33     -> 10.38.22.34     [ours]
    x4     ICMP t0/c0 10.38.22.34     -> 10.38.22.33     [ours]
```
**4 of 4 and 4 of 4.** The deletion was scoped to the interface it named; the box, the capture
and the DUT's IP stack are all demonstrably alive.

### 5c -- ADDITION, restoring the inherited underlay

```
awplus(config)#interface vlan48
awplus(config-if)#ip address 10.38.22.66/27
awplus(config-if)#end                                 [box 14:20:05 NZDT]
